{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Let us now pass through your land.</b> And he did not say ״נָא נַעְבְּרָה״ (״let us now pass״). If we interpret it as an expression of request, his intention was to attach the request to 'your land' — for that is the essence of the request, that the passage be through his land. And if we interpret it as an expression of time, it may be explained in accordance with what they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 44) — that one of the three nations that HaShem gave to the seed of Abraham is Edom. Therefore Moses was precise in this mission and said that all the conditions he stipulates upon himself — ״we will not turn aside to the right or to the left״ and so forth — all this applies only to the present passage; but when they pass in the time to come, for Moses is the one who will be the savior and master then, he will not accept upon himself any of the conditions, but rather to dispossess them, to rout them, and to plunder their spoil, as it is written (Obadiah 1): ״the house of Jacob shall be fire… and the house of Esau stubble…״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:24.773180263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}